  "id": "fact-retrieval",
  "term": "fact retrieval",
  "definition": "Fact retrieval is the recall of learned arithmetic facts from memory, such as multiplication answers, rather than working them out step by step. In this context, it refers to accessing number facts stored in an associative memory network, with children’s reliance on verbal versus visuo-spatial working memory changing over development.",
